  "question": {
    "text": "If the pair of straight lines $x^2-2 p x y-y^2=0$ and $x^2-2 p x y-y^2=0$ be such that each pair bisects the angle between the other pair, then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$p q=-1$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{p}=\\mathrm{q}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$p=-q$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{pq}=1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of bisector of both pair of straight lines,\n$p x^2+2 x y-p y^2=0$      <img src=\"assets\\st0204_f0872388e45f.png\"><br>\n$q x^2+2 x y-q y^2=0$<img src=\"assets\\st0204_44f5faf60fce.png\"><br>\nFrom (1) and (2).     $\\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{1}=\\frac{2}{-2 \\mathrm{p}}=\\frac{-\\mathrm{q}}{-1} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{pq}=-1$"
  }
}